\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord, I believe a rest remains
\par To all Thy people known,
\par A rest where pure enjoyment reigns,
\par And Thou art loved alone:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. A rest, where all our soul's desire
\par Is fixed on things above;
\par Where fear, and sin, and grief expire,
\par Cast out by perfect love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O that I now the rest might know,
\par Believe, and enter in!
\par Now, Saviour, now the bestow,
\par And let me cease from sin.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Remove this hardness from my heart,
\par This unbelief remove;
\par To me the rest of faith impart,
\par The sabbath of Thy love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. I would be Thine, Thou know'st I would,
\par And have Thee all my own;
\par Thee, O my all-sufficient Good!
\par I want, and Thee alone.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Thy name to me, Thy nature grant;
\par This, only this be given:
\par Nothing beside my God I want,
\par Nothing in earth or heaven.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

